# Shell scripts must always check out with LF line endings — a CRLF
# shebang line ("#!/usr/bin/env bash\r") fails to exec on Linux/macOS.
# Without this, Windows' core.autocrlf=true (a common default) silently
# converts scripts/run.sh to CRLF on checkout/commit, breaking it for
# every Linux user even though it looks fine in an editor on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf

# cargo fmt / cargo build always write Rust manifests and source with LF,
# regardless of platform. Without this, Windows' core.autocrlf=true keeps
# re-flagging desktop-app/src-tauri/Cargo.toml (and .rs files) as modified
# after every build even when the real content never changed — a false
# "dirty" signal git status has shown, unprompted, across multiple builds.
*.rs text eol=lf
Cargo.toml text eol=lf
Cargo.lock text eol=lf
